But note: beta preparation requires operator linked; we will assign operator to beta now and keep.

Thus we need to ensure operator is free before assigning to beta. It is free after destination lock release.

Thus steps:

- Prepare origin (create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness) -> no operator.
- Activate origin node.
- Lock origin (requires operator) -> assign operator, lock, then release.
- Prepare destination (create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness) -> no operator.
- Activate destination node.
- Lock destination (requires operator) -> assign operator, lock, then release.
- Detach task profiles from origin and destination (to make route_task_profile available for later).
- Assemble transport leg.
- Authorize loading (need origin_availability task profile linked; we need to attach task profile to origin again before authorize).
- Prepare beta: create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness, assign operator (keep), assign skill certificate.
- Load container onto leg for beta.
- Stage beta.
- Verify loading profile nominal for beta.
- Now beta has operator linked, skill linked, staged.

